language js(typescript)

// R6 + R8 — every field and method carries an explicit modifier.
//
// Constructors are exempt, and that is the house form rather than an oversight: not
// one of the eleven owner-written classes writes `public constructor`. COS-360 proved
// what enforcing it costs — nine errors, every one in a file the house style was
// recovered from.
//
// The exemption is free here. `JsConstructorClassMember` is its own node type, so
// naming the other four member kinds is what excludes it. Biome's native
// `useConsistentMemberAccessibility` has no equivalent escape hatch — its only option
// is `accessibility`, so switching it on would flag all eleven constructors and
// re-open the ruling COS-360 closed. That is why this rule is a plugin.
//
// The check is bound to `modifiers` rather than to the member as a whole. `contains`
// walks the entire subtree, so testing the member itself meant a `private` on some
// class declared *inside* a method body satisfied the check and suppressed the real
// violation on the method — a rule that silently exempts exactly the largest members.
//
// `$name <: not JsPrivateClassMemberName()` excludes `#field`. TypeScript rejects
// `private #x` outright (TS18010), so demanding a modifier there asks for something
// unwritable, and with no inline suppressions in this repo the first `#field` anyone
// added would make lint unpassable. The ESLint rule skipped them for the same reason.
// The two signature nodes cover `declare` fields and bare method overload signatures,
// which are their own node types and were invisible to the four concrete ones.
or {
    JsPropertyClassMember(modifiers = $modifiers, name = $name),
    JsMethodClassMember(modifiers = $modifiers, name = $name),
    JsGetterClassMember(modifiers = $modifiers, name = $name),
    JsSetterClassMember(modifiers = $modifiers, name = $name),
    TsPropertySignatureClassMember(modifiers = $modifiers, name = $name),
    TsMethodSignatureClassMember(modifiers = $modifiers, name = $name)
} as $member where {
    $modifiers <: not contains TsAccessibilityModifier(),
    $name <: not JsPrivateClassMemberName(),
    register_diagnostic(
        span = $member,
        message = "R6/R8: every field and method carries an explicit accessibility modifier."
    )
}
